    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "IMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFor Northwest Orient Airlines Passengers\nWE WANT YOU TO KNOW ABOUT CERTAIN SAFETY\nFEATURES OF THE ELECTRA II\nNORTHWEST ORIENT\nEMERGENCY EXITS\n6 exits are provided for your use. The chart below shows their\narrangement. The 3 black arrows indicate removable windows. 3 gray\narrows indicate door exits. The two rear doors are equipped with fast\noperating evacuation slides. 1 window has an escape rope.\nInflatable Evacuation Slide - ready to use.\nEMERSENCY\nEXIT\nESCAPE\nROPE\nUSEABLE\nIF STEPS\nCAN BE\nEXTENDED\nEVACUATION\nSLIDE\nEVACUATION\nSLIDE\nFLOOR PLAN OF\nELECTRA II\nDOOR EXITS\nWINDOW EXITS\nIllustration of Hand Held Evacuation Slide.\n(Gray Arrows)\nShown ready for use.\nPF-124\nRev. 9/69\nELECTRA II",
      "HOW TO OPERATE WINDOW EXITS FROM INSIDE\nSTEP 1.\nSTEP 2.\nBRACE POSITION\nTO OPEN REMOVE\nSHIELD COVERING\nRELEASE LEVER\nSTEP 3.\nREACH IN OPENING\nGRASP HANDLE AND\nPULL RELEASE LEVER\nSTEP 4\nPULL ENTIRE WINDOW\nINWARD\nGRASP SIDES,\nLIFT OUT AND PLACE\nON SEAT\nHand carried baggage must remain in the stowed area until the aircraft has come\nto a complete stop.\n2011.126.533"
    ],
